  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Land Systems has $1.8B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, across 369 awards and with an average award size of $4.7M. General Dynamics Land Systems obligations are up 14.8% year over year. General Dynamics Land Systems obligations by fiscal year show a peak at $4B in FY22 and a decline to $1.5B in FY25 before the current-year partial total of $1.8B. General Dynamics Land Systems is heavily concentrated in Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing with $1.6B in obligations. General Dynamics Land Systems also has smaller obligations in General Automotive Repair at $82.4M, Facilities Support Services at $34.3M, and Engineering Services at $18.9M. General Dynamics Land Systems has additional activity in Optical Instrument and Lens Manufacturing, Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing, and related manufacturing and services NAICS categories. General Dynamics Land Systems current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date and some award-value tables on the page report total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are General Dynamics Land Systems' obligations by market?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Land Systems is highly concentrated in one market. Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing accounts for $1.6B of obligations. General Dynamics Land Systems' next-largest market is General Automotive Repair at $82.4M, followed by Facilities Support Services at $34.3M and Engineering Services at $18.9M. The remaining listed markets each have single-digit millions in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How have General Dynamics Land Systems' annual obligations trended recently?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Land Systems obligations rose to $4B in FY22 then fell to $3.5B in FY23 and to $2.6B in FY24. General Dynamics Land Systems obligations declined further to $1.5B in FY25 and are $1.8B in FY26 to date. General Dynamics Land Systems year-over-year obligations are up 14.8% for the current fiscal-year-to-date period."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
